{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "kjv-proverbs-030",
  "collection": "kjv-bible",
  "document_type": "bible_chapter",
  "number": 30,
  "title": "Proverbs 30",
  "display_title": "Proverbs 30",
  "translation": "King James Version",
  "translationCode": "KJV",
  "bookId": "proverbs",
  "book": "Proverbs",
  "bookName": "Proverbs",
  "bookOrder": 20,
  "testament": "old",
  "chapter": 30,
  "sortOrder": 20030,
  "verseCount": 33,
  "aliases": [
    "Prov",
    "Pr",
    "Prv"
  ],
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "The words of Agur the son of Jakeh, even the prophecy: the man spake unto Ithiel, even unto Ithiel and Ucal,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "Surely I am more brutish than any man, and have not the understanding of a man.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "I neither learned wisdom, nor have the knowledge of the holy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Who hath ascended up into heaven, or descended? who hath gathered the wind in his fists? who hath bound the waters in a garment? who hath established all the ends of the earth? what is his name, and what is his son’s name, if thou canst tell?",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "Every word of God is pure: he is a shield unto them that put their trust in him.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "Add thou not unto his words, lest he reprove thee, and thou be found a liar.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "Two things have I required of thee; deny me them not before I die:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "Remove far from me vanity and lies: give me neither poverty nor riches; feed me with food convenient for me:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "Lest I be full, and deny thee, and say, Who is the LORD? or lest I be poor, and steal, and take the name of my God in vain.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "Accuse not a servant unto his master, lest he curse thee, and thou be found guilty.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:10"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-011",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 11,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:11",
      "numberLabel": "11",
      "text": "There is a generation that curseth their father, and doth not bless their mother.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:11",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:11"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-012",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 12,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:12",
      "numberLabel": "12",
      "text": "There is a generation that are pure in their own eyes, and yet is not washed from their filthiness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:12",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:12"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-013",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 13,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:13",
      "numberLabel": "13",
      "text": "There is a generation, O how lofty are their eyes! and their eyelids are lifted up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:13",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:13"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-014",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 14,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:14",
      "numberLabel": "14",
      "text": "There is a generation, whose teeth are as swords, and their jaw teeth as knives, to devour the poor from off the earth, and the needy from among men.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:14",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:14"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-015",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 15,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:15",
      "numberLabel": "15",
      "text": "The horseleach hath two daughters, crying, Give, give. There are three things that are never satisfied, yea, four things say not, It is enough:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:15",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:15"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-016",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 16,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:16",
      "numberLabel": "16",
      "text": "The grave; and the barren womb; the earth that is not filled with water; and the fire that saith not, It is enough.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:16",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:16"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-017",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 17,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:17",
      "numberLabel": "17",
      "text": "The eye that mocketh at his father, and despiseth to obey his mother, the ravens of the valley shall pick it out, and the young eagles shall eat it.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:17",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:17"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-018",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 18,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:18",
      "numberLabel": "18",
      "text": "There be three things which are too wonderful for me, yea, four which I know not:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:18",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:18"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-019",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 19,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:19",
      "numberLabel": "19",
      "text": "The way of an eagle in the air; the way of a serpent upon a rock; the way of a ship in the midst of the sea; and the way of a man with a maid.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:19",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-020",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 20,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:20",
      "numberLabel": "20",
      "text": "Such is the way of an adulterous woman; she eateth, and wipeth her mouth, and saith, I have done no wickedness.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:20",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:20"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-021",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 21,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:21",
      "numberLabel": "21",
      "text": "For three things the earth is disquieted, and for four which it cannot bear:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:21",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:21"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-022",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 22,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:22",
      "numberLabel": "22",
      "text": "For a servant when he reigneth; and a fool when he is filled with meat;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:22",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:22"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-023",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 23,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:23",
      "numberLabel": "23",
      "text": "For an odious woman when she is married; and an handmaid that is heir to her mistress.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:23",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:23"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-024",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 24,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:24",
      "numberLabel": "24",
      "text": "There be four things which are little upon the earth, but they are exceeding wise:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:24",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:24"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-025",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 25,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:25",
      "numberLabel": "25",
      "text": "The ants are a people not strong, yet they prepare their meat in the summer;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:25",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:25"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-026",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 26,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:26",
      "numberLabel": "26",
      "text": "The conies are but a feeble folk, yet make they their houses in the rocks;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:26",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:26"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-027",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 27,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:27",
      "numberLabel": "27",
      "text": "The locusts have no king, yet go they forth all of them by bands;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:27",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:27"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-028",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 28,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:28",
      "numberLabel": "28",
      "text": "The spider taketh hold with her hands, and is in kings’ palaces.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:28",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:28"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-029",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 29,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:29",
      "numberLabel": "29",
      "text": "There be three things which go well, yea, four are comely in going:",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:29",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:29"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-030",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 30,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:30",
      "numberLabel": "30",
      "text": "A lion which is strongest among beasts, and turneth not away for any;",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:30",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:30"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-031",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 31,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:31",
      "numberLabel": "31",
      "text": "A greyhound; an he goat also; and a king, against whom there is no rising up.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:31",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:31"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-032",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 32,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:32",
      "numberLabel": "32",
      "text": "If thou hast done foolishly in lifting up thyself, or if thou hast thought evil, lay thine hand upon thy mouth.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:32",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:32"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-033",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 33,
      "verseId": "kjv:proverbs:30:33",
      "numberLabel": "33",
      "text": "Surely the churning of milk bringeth forth butter, and the wringing of the nose bringeth forth blood: so the forcing of wrath bringeth forth strife.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Proverbs 30:33",
        "verseKey": "kjv:proverbs:30:33"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
